Z||000000||Joe4x4||03-31-2001||06:55 PM||||Hi everyone..... my girlfriend and I are loooking  to put a bid on a house.<BR>What should I look out for?<BR>What games should I play ? (bid low and work are way up)<P>Any info? first house ...What type of loan  should I be looking for?<BR>I`m thinking conventional would be best .(no PIMI) as in FHA.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Need For Speed........<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/car1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierospeeder||03-31-2001||11:56 PM||||I would get an inspection on the house.  Its like a mechanic for a house.<P>To tell you everything what might be wrong with it.  Unless your like norm abram and can fix anything.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tina||04-01-2001||11:08 AM||||Check neighborhood on the way down, or up?<BR>Any mayor construction planned ?<BR>aka.Highway, shopping mall (increased traffic, noise)<BR>Look at neighbor houses,average price of houses in neighborhood? <BR>Any other houses in the same neighborhood for <BR>sale? (Play one against the other)<BR>How long has the house been on the market?<BR>(the longer the better for bargaining)<BR>School districts? Levy-plans in the future?<BR>Real estate taxes in comparision with different neighborhoods.<BR>My advise: Get a good real estate agent,buy <BR>a real fixxer upper in the best neighborhood,<BR>and watch the value of your house grow as you fix it.<BR>(Norm Abrahms talents required)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>If I left anything out, been awhile. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Refer to good REAL ESTATE AGENT.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Happy hunting, and good luck.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Joe4x4||04-01-2001||08:36 PM||||Thanks for the advice.<P>The house is nice , the thing that is getting me is that it is apraised at 108,000<BR>and she bought it at 128,000 4 months ago.<BR>She is trying to sell it at 139,900.<P>We are gonna put a bid in at 110,000.(monday)<BR>I guess play the #`s game.<BR>We think that we will not go above what she payed for it.<P>What do you think ?<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/egg_harbor_city.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>Need For Speed........<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/car1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||KRMFiero||04-01-2001||09:49 PM||||If she payed more then its valued at, and she is trying to sell it for more then she paided  did she put anything into the house what would be worth the extra 20k?<P>How much land is with the house? ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||04-01-2001||09:56 PM||||If the appraisal if for the tax rolls - you can't go by that.||||reg||1
Z||000006||LarryB||04-01-2001||10:23 PM||||Phil's right.  You can't go by the value assessed for tax purposes.  Also remember that the real estate agent works for the seller, not the buyer.  <P>Since you're buying this with your girlfriend (i.e. she's not your wife) you might want to consider entering a contract spelling out what happens if you two break up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> It's an unpleasant thought but if it happens things can turn ugly. <P>One last thing, make sure that if you agree on something staying (washer/dryer, fridge, light fixtures, etc. etc.) it is included in the written P&S agreement.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by LarryB (edited 04-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||ray b||04-01-2001||10:52 PM||||location location location = $$$$$<BR>learn value of property in difffert<BR>locations can be 2x 3x 4x more for same<BR>house in good or bad location.<BR>who built it, when was it built, union men?<BR>value up or down on that house depends on who set price just like on a car you get the <BR>best deal from fools so look for sale by owners who don't know what they got, agents<BR>suck avoid like plage.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Old Lar||04-02-2001||04:30 PM||||I agree with LarryB that buying a house with a GF is more risky than buying one with a wife.  Have it all spelled out up front what will happen when (if) a breakup occurs.  You both will be individually responsible for the debt and if one flys the coupe, the remainding partner is responsible for all.  If you can afford $110K on your own, go for it.  If you need that second income think twice.  Bankruptcy is not the way out of debt.||||reg||2
Z||000009||rogergarrison||04-02-2001||06:24 PM||||get at least a 4 car garage, check outside auto storage law, lol.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Joe4x4||04-03-2001||10:48 AM||||thanks guys ....I know what you guys are saying. I was thinking that , and if we do go are own way , I`ll be able to pay the loan. (Do Not See That Happening).<BR>My girlfriend and I work the same shift,<BR>and we have the same brake,and we live together. LOL  YES 24-7-365.<BR>We are like glue. We have been seeing each other for over 2 years now.<P>thanks again....Joe<P>------------------<BR>Need For Speed........<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/car1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||Oreif||04-03-2001||11:46 AM||||I would get the house appraised by a local appraiser. They take into account everything. The tax appraisal isn't the real value. If they bought the house 4 months ago they definitely won't take less than they paid. They have only paid back about $100 of the original mortgage at the most. They won't lose $18,000 + real estate agent fees to sell you the house. If the house is being sold thru an agency the asking price is probably close to the actual value of the house. (slightly higher or lower). You may get it for $135,000 but I don't think you'll get it for any less than that. Also why are they selling after only 4 months? Loss of income? or was the house an investment purchase? (meaning did they buy the house to repair/fix-up then sell for a profit) When buying a house there are many things to look at. My advise is take your time and look at everything. We looked at probably 50-70 houses before we bought ours.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Taijiguy||04-04-2001||01:12 PM||||When it comes to the inspection, get an inspector who will work for you as the buyer, not the seller.<BR>And in general, get the cheapest house in the neighborhood, you never want the most expensive house in the neighborhood.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Joe4x4||04-04-2001||08:29 PM||||Tue 4/4/01 We put a bid in at $115,000.<BR>She is selling  because she does not like the 1 1/2 hr drive to and from work .<BR>She thought that she would not mind,...she found out that the drive she does not like.<BR>So she want`s to find a house closer to work.<P>Will let you know what happens.<P>Again thanks.......Joe||||reg||1
